  checks so far: lambda_1 closed form PASS; monotone approach PASS; K1 PASS; K2 PASS; K3 TRIGGERED

--- HONEST LIMITS (stated as required) ---
  1. Partial sums over N = 500..2000 zeros are NOT a proof of RH: the tail
     beyond N is controlled here NUMERICALLY (exact power sums + Nielandt-
     type envelope) -- numerical control, not a proof.
  2. n = 1..50 only; Li's criterion requires ALL n.  Oesterle (unpubl., via
     Bombieri-Lagarias 1999 p.441, relayed by Maslanka 2004): zeros on the
     line up to height T give Li positivity only up to about n ~ T^..; the
     verified range does not decide RH.
  3. The exact lambda_n come from a numerical Taylor extraction (dps 80, 512
     points, FFT); analytically exact in principle, numerically verified by
     monotone partial-sum approach and by the lambda_1 closed form.
  4. NO PROOF OF RH IS CLAIMED.  RH is unproven; this lane reports numerical
     evidence (true lambda_n > 0, n <= 50) and a framework-compatibility
     statistic for the ladder (the positivity of the synthetic path).

  runtime 268 s | N_eff = 2000 | dps = 80 (exact route)

